<title>LATVIA: SAULES BANK ALLOWED TO CONDUCT VOUCHER ACTIVITIES.</title>
<headline>SAULES BANK ALLOWED TO CONDUCT VOUCHER ACTIVITIES.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's Saules Bank said on Wednesday that it had received a license from the Economy Ministry to carry out transactions with privatisation vouchers.</p>
<p>The bank also said in a statement that it was allowed to accept voucher accounts. </p>
<p>The vouchers have been distributed to the population to enable ordinary Latvians to buy stakes in state-run firms.</p>
<p>Saules Bank is Latvia's ninth largest bank.</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Riga news room +371 721 52 40</p>
